    "Description": "### Impact\n\n`sanitizeFilter` is Mongoose's mechanism for protecting against query selector injection attacks. In older versions of Mongoose, `sanitizeFilter` was not applied for `countDocuments()` queries.\n\n### Patches\n\nPatches have been released for all supported Mongoose major release lines. Please upgrade to the following versions depending on which major version of Mongoose applications are using.\n\n1. `^9.9.2`\n2. `^8.24.3`\n3. `^7.8.12`\n4. `^6.13.11`\n\n### Workarounds\n\nMiddleware:\n\n```javascript\nmongoose.plugin(function() {\n  schema.pre('countDocuments', function() {\n    // This will always apply `sanitizeFilter` on `countDocuments`\n    mongoose.sanitizeFilter(this.getFilter());\n  });\n});\n```",
    "Origin": "UNSPECIFIED",
    "PublishedAt": "2026-11-10T19:37:32Z",
    "Severity": "CRITICAL",
    "Summary": "Mongoose: sanitizeFilter not applied on countDocuments",
